@node Multi-Target
@chapter Multi-Target Support
@cindex multi-target
@findex ENABLE_MULTI_TARGET

A multi-target build links several complete backends into one
compiler: one @command{cc1} (and one @file{libgccjit}) carries the
configured target and a set of secondary targets, and each invocation
compiles for exactly one of them.  The driver selects with
@option{--target=}, the compiler proper with @option{-fmulti-target=},
and a JIT context with @code{gcc_jit_context_set_target}.  The mode is
opt-in: it exists only under @option{--enable-multi-target}, every
change in shared code sits behind @code{ENABLE_MULTI_TARGET}, and a
default build compiles byte-identically to one that predates the
feature.

This chapter describes the internals for maintainers: how the build
composes several targets, what the shared ``union'' surface is, how a
backend is described and activated at runtime, and what a port must
satisfy to participate.

